# Rovas work for Rovas agents

When Civic needs **Rovas-side** changes (new/changed Services resources, OAuth,
Drupal rules, `/rovas/*` payloads, claim registry, deploy notes for rovdev):

1. **Write the task for the Rovas agent** in
   `~/Documents/homeProjects/rovas/docs/integration/civic.md`
   — that file is the source of truth for agents working in the **rovas** repo.
2. Add or update a **Next work:** section (checklist + smoke test + response
   shape). Link it from the agents TOC at the top of that doc.
3. Keep Civic-side notes in `docs/rovas-integration.md` (Expo + Civic API).
   Mention the Rovas **Next work** title; do not duplicate the full Rovas
   implementation checklist here.
4. Do **not** rely on chat history alone — if Rovas must build something, it
   must be written into `rovas/docs/integration/civic.md` so a Rovas agent can
   pick it up without this conversation.

Civic agents implement Expo/API clients against that contract; Rovas agents
implement the Drupal side from that doc.
